<title>UK: Baltic, Black Sea exports rise 163,000 bpd on week.</title>
<headline>Baltic, Black Sea exports rise 163,000 bpd on week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals rose 162,761 barrels per day (bpd) in the third week of March from the previous week to 1.89 million bpd, Petro-Logistics said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The total was 93,926 bpd higher than the same week last year.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from Baltic and Black Sea ports rose 101,763 bpd on the week to 1.02 million bpd, which is just below year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports rose 86,632 bpd to 561,083 bpd but still lagged year-ago levels by 43,140 bpd.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports fell 67,142 bpd to 212,173 bpd but were 65,954 bpd higher than in the same week last year.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro-Logistics lists a breakdown in metric tonnes of petroleum exports from the Baltic and Black Sea in the third week of March.</p>
